Subject: [PATCH 082/148] hjviewer: support codes from staff (W1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The client side of docs/access-tickets.md 3-7 (the hjviewer repo's
v182/w1-server): a logged-in staff member makes a one-time support code,
and the PC of someone who is not logged in trades it for its own ticket.

- PC side (P3): P1's notice gets [지원 코드 넣기] while GET
  /api/hjv/access says "codes":true (1.8.0's server never does), and its
  text and the ID card's line name the support code then. Its dialog
  "지원 코드" takes XXXX-XXXX, checks the form as hjv-api's support::read
  does (E6 at once, nothing sent), and [연결] goes with the busy bar of
  the access password's dialog (U07), the keyboard's submit, no autofill
  or suggestions. E2, E5 as the access password's, E6, E7, E8 for the
  rest. A ticket shows as P2 does, the home line "지원 코드로 연결을 받는
  중 · …까지" (two hours), [끝내기] and the window's close ask alike.
- Core: guest.rs trades a code through the access password's seam
  (set "hjv-guest-pc-code", get "hjv-guest-result:pc-code"): sealed with
  "p":"code" in the request's "code" member, signed as the PC's request,
  sent once more as it was when no answer came (hjv-api answers the same
  body with its first answer), the ticket in the access password's place
  in the process that registers. read_code ports hjv-api's read.
  hjv-e2e: --hjv-e2e-guest-pc-code <code> and --hjv-e2e-support-code.
- Creator (S1, S2): the account module learns "support_code":true from
  the login answer's and currentUser's hjv (hjv-support-code), and
  support.rs makes a code with the login's signed request
  (set "hjv-support-code-make", get "hjv-support-code-result", read
  once). [지원 코드 만들기] shows only then: Settings → Account on the
  desktop and the phone, and above the 내 PC tab's list. The dialog shows
  the code large with the time left counting down, [코드 복사], [안내문
  복사], S8 on a server that checks nobody, the expired state with [다시
  만들기], and S5 to S7; a 401 ends the login as the account requests'
  401 does.
- Tests: the request bodies, the seal, the code's form (hjv-api's
  vectors), hjv-api's answers to a maker, the flag (Rust); the texts, the
  form, the flags' effects, the countdown and the error mapping (Dart).

